From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Buildroot Demo <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 23:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] stm32f429-disco: disable unwired OTG HS ULPI clock

The STM32F429 Discovery USB USER connector uses the OTG HS controller with
its embedded full-speed PHY.  It has no external ULPI PHY or ULPI clock.

The board clock setup enables nearly every AHB1 peripheral, including the
OTGHSULPI clock gate.  Linux probes DWC2 before unused clocks are disabled;
with OTGHSULPIEN still set, the first DWC2 core reset never completes even
after selecting the embedded PHY.

Keep the OTGHS core clock enabled but explicitly disable its unused ULPI
clock.  This matches the STM32CubeF4 USB device reference configuration for
the board.

Signed-off-by: Buildroot Demo <noreply@example.com>
---
 stm32f429i-disco.c | 6 ++++++
 stm32f4_regs.h     | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/stm32f429i-disco.c b/stm32f429i-disco.c
index da35904..4999565 100644
--- a/stm32f429i-disco.c
+++ b/stm32f429i-disco.c
@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@ static void clock_setup(void)
 	*RCC_AHB1ENR |= 0x7ef417ff;
 	*RCC_AHB2ENR |= 0xf1;
 	*RCC_AHB3ENR |= 0x1;
+
+	/*
+	 * USB USER uses the OTG HS embedded FS PHY.  No external ULPI PHY is
+	 * wired, and leaving its clock gate enabled prevents a DWC2 reset.
+	 */
+	*RCC_AHB1ENR &= ~RCC_AHB1ENR_OTGHSULPIEN;
 	*RCC_APB1ENR |= 0xf6fec9ff;
 	*RCC_APB2ENR |= 0x4777f33;
 
diff --git a/stm32f4_regs.h b/stm32f4_regs.h
index f9646ea..403bc58 100644
--- a/stm32f4_regs.h
+++ b/stm32f4_regs.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #define RCC_DCKCFGR_SDIO48	(1 << 28)
 
 #define RCC_AHB1ENR_GPIOGEN	(1 << 6)
+#define RCC_AHB1ENR_OTGHSULPIEN	(1 << 30)
 
 #define RCC_AHB1LPENR_OTGHSULPILPEN	(1 << 30)
 
-- 
2.39.5
